- op: discuss  # 860d
  at: '2026-08-22T00:05:47Z'  # 860d
  by: agent  # 860d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 860d
  clock: 3  # 860d
  nonce: 860d  # 860d
  message: "SECOND AND THIRD INSTANCES, IN A DIFFERENT FILE, SO THIS IS A CLASS AND NOT ONE TEST.\n2026-08-21, observed while running check-package-coverage for INV-rozob. Both are in\npackages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests/test_compile_properties.py, not test_tui.py:\n\n    run 1: FAILED TestCompileProperties::test_idempotency\n    run 2: FAILED TestCompileProperties::test_permutation_invariance\n\nSame signature as this item's original: NEITHER REPRODUCES IN ISOLATION. Immediately\nafter each failure, on the same tree:\n\n    python3 -m pytest .../test_compile_properties.py -q -p no:randomly  -> 6 passed\n    python3 -m pytest .../test_compile_properties.py::TestCompileProperties::\\\n        test_idempotency -q -p no:randomly                              -> 1 passed\n\nSo the failing set is not stable across runs either -- two different tests failed on two\nconsecutive full-package runs of the same code. That rules out \"one bad assertion\" and\npoints at shared mutable state or ordering between tests in the tracker package, which\nis a different mechanism from the TUI dismiss-callback timing this item was filed on.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND NOISE, and it is the same argument this item already makes: these\nare the failures that redden `check-package-coverage` and the cron aggregate, and an\nagent that has learned to read a tracker-package red as \"probably the flake\" will read a\nREAL tracker regression the same way. I did exactly that twice today before checking.\n\nNOT DIAGNOSED: whether the compile-properties flakes and the TUI flake share a cause\n(both are in the tracker package, but a Textual dismiss-callback race and a\nproperty-test permutation failure have no obvious common mechanism); whether\n`-p no:randomly` in the isolation runs masks the ordering that triggers it -- the\nisolation check should be re-run WITHOUT that flag before concluding order-dependence."  # 860d
- op: discuss  # 4ade
  at: '2026-09-25T18:00:44Z'  # 4ade
  by: agent  # 4ade
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4ade
  clock: 4  # 4ade
  nonce: 4ade  # 4ade
  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). A FIX FOR THIS ROW'S MECHANISM LANDED AFTER ITS LAST UPDATE, and the row does not record it. Status unchanged.\n\n2f2f79ff8d (2026-08-30, \"fix(tracker): the modal test harness must fail its wait, not return (INV-bozid)\") changes `_wait_for_modal` in packages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests/test_tui.py in two ways:\n (1) it RAISES on exhaustion, naming the widget and the wait, instead of returning as if it had succeeded;\n (2) it waits for LAYOUT (a non-zero region), not DOM presence. A zero-sized region explains exactly this row's `'NOT_SET' is None` sentinel: the click lands nowhere, so the dismiss callback never runs.\nThe commit states it is NOT reproducible locally and fits the CI co-residency picture.\n\nCurrent signal: the latest cron full-suite (615471e2, 2026-09-25) has test-all-packages OK. I did NOT walk the cron history since 08-30 for a recurrence, so \"no recurrence\" is unverified.\n\nClose condition suggestion: a walk of the full-suite cron verdicts since 2f2f79ff8d with zero test_tui failures. Or, if it recurs, the new message now names what was waited for. Either can be read off `ci-debug` without a local repro."  # 4ade
- op: discuss  # c605
  at: '2026-10-01T00:58:24Z'  # c605
  by: agent  # c605
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c605
  clock: 5  # c605
  nonce: c605  # c605
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): PARTLY-DONE. Plausible fixes for both filed shapes have landed; neither has been confirmed by a loaded run, and one load-sensitive path remains in the compile-properties half.\n- TUI half (the filed instance): 2f2f79ff8d (2026-08-30) rewrote _wait_for_modal (test_tui.py:2608-2658). It now waits for a non-zero laid-out size of #modal-dialog and RAISES on exhaustion. The filed test is TestLockScreenUnit::test_cancel_returns_none at test_tui.py:3262. Not addressed: after pilot.click(\"#cancel\") each test still does one pilot.pause() before asserting _result. Under load, a dismiss callback that needs more than one tick would still read 'NOT_SET'. This is a hypothesis from reading the code, not a repro.\n- compile-properties half (discussion 1): 86bf3b9a41 (2026-09-25) suppressed HealthCheck.too_slow on the file's four properties (test_compile_properties.py:157-164) after a 0.94 s draw failed the 8.1.0 release-check. That matches \"fails only under load\". Not addressed: Hypothesis's per-example deadline is still the default 200 ms (hypothesis 6.151.6; no deadline= in the file or a tracker conftest profile). So a loaded run can still raise DeadlineExceeded/Flaky. The 08-21 failure messages were not recorded, so it is unknown whether they were too_slow, deadline or a property failure.\n- No commits to test_compile_properties.py or tracker compile code since 08-21 besides 86bf3b9a41.\n- RELATED, not linked: WI-balap (TestBeforeScreenUnit::test_empty_submit_returns_none, same _wait_for_modal harness, order-dependent under pytest-randomly). 2f2f79ff8d applies to it too.\n- NOT RUN (forbidden in this pass). What would confirm it: a walk of the full-suite cron verdicts since 2f2f79ff8d with zero tracker-package failures (ci-debug), PLUS at least one local loaded run (`check-package-coverage`, or the tracker package under -n auto beside a full suite) with no failures in test_tui.py or test_compile_properties.py. Record the randomly seed.\nPROPOSED: add WI-balap to this row's related items, or say that the two are one family. Consider settings(deadline=None) on the four properties, the same rationale as 86bf3b9a41."  # c605
