  set:  # 8a3a
    description: "FOUND WHILE REFUTING INV-bobor'S ROOT CAUSE, 2026-08-21. This was the live cause of\nINV-bozid's masking half: one intermittent assertion turned the whole twice-daily\nwhole-codebase signal red, which is why a correctly-detected security-claim regression\nsat unread.\n\nOBSERVED IN CI, fetched log, cron firing 2026-08-20 13:00 UTC, tip f7d88b98e7, step\ntest-all-packages:\n\n    FAILED packages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests/test_tui.py::TestLockScreenUnit::\n      test_cancel_returns_none - AssertionError: assert 'NOT_SET' is None\n    = 1 failed, 23210 passed, 31 skipped, 17 xfailed, 428 warnings in 935.34s\n\nIt does not reproduce in isolation (3 of 3 single-test runs passed on 6e290fcdb8), and the\n2026-08-21 13:00 cron firing was green. So it is a property of the loaded run, and the\naggregate flickered between firings, which trains readers to ignore it.\n\nA SECOND SHAPE, SAME PACKAGE (2026-08-21, during check-package-coverage). Two consecutive\nfull tracker-package runs failed DIFFERENT tests in test_compile_properties.py\n(TestCompileProperties::test_idempotency, then ::test_permutation_invariance). Both passed\nin isolation, but only with -p no:randomly, so order-dependence was not separated from\nload. The failure messages were not recorded.\n\nFIXES LANDED, NEITHER CONFIRMED BY A LOADED RUN:\n  * TUI: 2f2f79ff8d (2026-08-30). _wait_for_modal (test_tui.py ~2608) now waits until\n    #modal-dialog has a non-zero laid-out size, and RAISES on exhaustion instead of\n    returning silently. A zero-sized region explains the 'NOT_SET' sentinel: the click\n    lands nowhere, so the dismiss callback never runs. The filed test is at test_tui.py ~3262.\n  * compile-properties: 86bf3b9a41 (2026-09-25) suppressed HealthCheck.too_slow on the\n    file's four properties, after one 0.94 s draw under a full -n auto suite failed the\n    8.1.0 release-check.\n\nREMAINING HAZARDS (from reading the code, not from repros):\n  * After pilot.click(\"#cancel\"), each modal test does one pilot.pause() before asserting\n    _result. A dismiss callback that needs more than one tick under load would still\n    read 'NOT_SET'.\n  * Hypothesis's per-example deadline is still the 200 ms default (no deadline= in the\n    file or a tracker conftest profile). A loaded run can still raise\n    DeadlineExceeded/Flaky. Candidate: settings(deadline=None), on the same rationale as\n    86bf3b9a41.\n\nRELATED: WI-balap (TestBeforeScreenUnit::test_empty_submit_returns_none, order-dependent\nunder pytest-randomly) uses the same _wait_for_modal harness, and 2f2f79ff8d applies to\nit as well. WI-kogop shares the class (a test-isolation leak that CI's distribution\nexposes or hides) but not the mechanism.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION: (1) a walk of the full-suite cron verdicts since 2f2f79ff8d (ci-debug)\nwith zero tracker-package failures, AND (2) at least one local loaded run\n(check-package-coverage, or the tracker package under -n auto beside a full suite) with no\nfailures in test_tui.py or test_compile_properties.py, with the pytest-randomly seed\nrecorded.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 8a3a
- op: discuss  # 0ff5
  at: '2026-10-01T03:51:04Z'  # 0ff5
  by: agent  # 0ff5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0ff5
  clock: 7  # 0ff5
  nonce: 0ff5  # 0ff5
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-09-30 (concurrent run). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/ruhul-wait-on-condition, commit c29495301b, LOCAL only (no push, no PR). Test-only change; no source files touched. Status unchanged.\n\nTUI HALF, the hazard the premise check named, now built and pinned. Mechanism, from reading Textual 7.5.0: a click's dismiss result is several queue hops after the click (Click -> Button -> Pressed bubbling to the screen -> dismiss -> app.call_next(callback)). Pilot.pause ends in wait_for_idle, which treats the process as idle when its CPU time stops advancing against wall-clock time. A worker descheduled on a loaded box matches that, so pause can return after one loop iteration.\nModel repro (scratch script, LockScreen, Pilot.pause patched to one asyncio.sleep(0)): click #cancel or #submit, one pause, read app._result -> 'NOT_SET' 8 of 8 for each button, which is the filed sentinel. The result arrives 3 ticks later. A milder model (wait_for_idle returning at once, _wait_for_screen intact) gave 'NOT_SET' on 2 of 5 clicks; escape presses were never affected.\nFix: _ModalTestApp._capture sets an asyncio.Event, and _wait_for_dismissal(app) awaits it (30 s bound, raises a named AssertionError on exhaustion). All 41 modal unit tests that assert a dismissal result use it, including TestLockScreenUnit::test_cancel_returns_none and WI-balap's TestBeforeScreenUnit::test_empty_submit_returns_none. TestWaitForDismissalHelper adds three tests: a REACH test (the old read gives 'NOT_SET' under the model), the helper returning under the model for #cancel and #submit, and the helper raising when nothing dismisses.\n\nCOMPILE-PROPERTIES HALF. The four properties share settings(max_examples=50, deadline=None, suppress_health_check=[too_slow]) and are now MODULE-LEVEL functions. As methods, calling them from a second self trips Hypothesis's differing_executors health check, which my first attempt hit. TestPropertiesSurviveASlowExample makes compile_ops sleep 0.3 s on its first call. Under the default deadline (mutation) all four fail with FlakyFailure wrapping DeadlineExceeded; with the fix all four pass. Whether the 08-21 failures were this mechanism is NOT known: their messages were not kept.\n\nEVIDENCE: targeted smart-test through the board, 9 files: RED 4 failed (NameError on the missing helper); GREEN 685 passed, 0 failed. pytest-randomly is NOT installed in this venv (ModuleNotFoundError), so these runs have no randomly seed.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION NOT MET, and not attempted. (1) No cron walk: ci-debug has no forge credential in a worktree, and the run forbids working in the main checkout. (2) No loaded run: check-package-coverage and full-suite runs are forbidden in this run and belong to integration.\n\nRESIDUALS: WI-zolin-sikot-hadov-zugif-sasug-bufub-fapab-mudul (new, P3) covers the TrackerApp integration modal tests, 38 click sites with the same hazard. Under the model the discuss submit mock reads 0 calls 4 of 4, and the cancel/not-called tests pass vacuously. Notes were also posted on WI-lotig (tests/test_transcript_pipeline_properties.py still uses the default deadline) and WI-balap."  # 0ff5
